int out onto our laps out  of effectively nowhere all the while we  were expecting just another slice of  life chapter or episode  and this is not where this one ends  either just barely succeeding to get out  of this strange ghost dimension thanks  to the quick thinking and  nerves of rohan josuke is brought up to  speed on everything however  since this serial killer in question  isn't a confirmed stand user  he concludes that it's a job for the  police which is fair considering they've  been looking for  this looming evil over the town in the  form of a stand user all of this time so  it stands to reason  they want to remain focused and that's  when the manga does something  i really wasn't prepared for they  immediately revealed  the killer driving home from work  talking to someone in the passenger seat  makes small talk with his passenger  before he attempts to help her out of  the car seat  and that's when the camera pans out to  reveal a severed hand  the way he talks to it caresses it and  uses it for  whatever reason really stayed with me  and truly horrified me but what i found  interesting more than perhaps anything  else was how araki saw fit to structure  this particular encounter  his viewers now know who the killer is  almost immediately after finding out  that there was one  but no one else does this turned out to  be  a spectacular decision for later on  shigechi's harvest  once again we are greeted by another  standalone seven chapter story  introducing us to a new member of the  morio community called  shigechi pretty much taking the focus in  this section is relationship and overall  dynamic between the  at first seemingly sweet and innocent  shigechi and the duo of josuke  and okuyatsu short on money once they  learn of shigechi's stand power harvest  and its unique abilities they see an  opportunity to leverage their ideas with  his ability to get some quick cash  the plans go perfectly according to  josuke's plan  however unable to see josuk'